== (2) the map rho(r) = 3r + lsb(r) ==
 r_l = 2^(d_l) m_l = 3^l n + S_(l-1) for all odd n <= 2000 and l <= 200: OK
 every n <= 100000 reaches a power of two under rho (max steps 129); once r is a power of two, rho(r) = 4r stays one
 n = 27: r_l = [27, 82, 248, 752, 2272, 6848] ... reaches 1180591620717411303424 = 2^70 after 41 steps; odd parts [27, 41, 31, 47, 71, 107, 161, 121, 91, 137, 103, 155] ...
== (3) best lower approximations of log_2 3 and the gaps 3^p - 2^A ==
 A/p =   1/  1 = 1.0000000   3^p - 2^A = 1
 A/p =   3/  2 = 1.5000000   3^p - 2^A = 1
 A/p =  11/  7 = 1.5714286   3^p - 2^A = 139
 A/p =  19/ 12 = 1.5833333   3^p - 2^A = 7153
 A/p =  84/ 53 = 1.5849057   3^p - 2^A = 4.043e+22
 A/p = 569/359 = 1.5849582   3^p - 2^A = 2.061e+168
 integer negative cycles occur at 1/1 (gap 1, x = -1), 3/2 (gap 1, x = -5), 11/7 (gap 139, x = -17); 19/12 (gap 7153) has none (necklace search p <= 12, S12 audit)
== (4) E_inf cap Z_<0 for |n| <= 10^6: negative odd n whose orbit never decreases in absolute value ==
 members: [-1, -5, -17]
== (5) the two-place identity on 27, -1, -5 ==
 n = 27: 2^(d_l) m_l / 3^l = n C_l and S_(l-1)/3^l = n (C_l - 1) exact for l <= 24; real partial sums S/3^l: ['0.3333', '0.5556', '0.8519', '1.0494', '1.1811'] ... ['2.0838', '2.1066', '2.1370']
 n = -1: 2^(d_l) m_l / 3^l = n C_l and S_(l-1)/3^l = n (C_l - 1) exact for l <= 24; real partial sums S/3^l: ['0.3333', '0.5556', '0.7037', '0.8025', '0.8683'] ... ['0.9999', '0.9999', '0.9999']
 n = -5: 2^(d_l) m_l / 3^l = n C_l and S_(l-1)/3^l = n (C_l - 1) exact for l <= 24; real partial sums S/3^l: ['0.3333', '0.5556', '0.8519', '1.0494', '1.3128'] ... ['3.6314', '3.7226', '3.7834']
 (27 reaches 1: C_l -> infinity, the real series diverges; -1 and -5 are cycle points: the real sums converge to -n, the 2-adic sums too)
